            <div xml:id="d895">

                <pb facs="0828" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00/244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Arnold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-07T17:00:00-05:56"><hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 8—5:13
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Revolutionary activities of Arturo Araujo were discovered and the President
                    ordered his arrest and [that] of his father Eugenio Araujo. Troops sent this
                    morning to arrest Arturo at his plantation were fired upon. He escaped from the
                    plantation. Martial law proclaimed 11 a.m. today. Eugenio imprisoned yesterday
                    afternoon in Salvador. President informs me that he has the situation well in
                    hand.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arnold</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
